{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>What is this that Elohim has done to us.</b> If our brother is imprisoned, it is just, on account of Joseph our brother whose distress of soul we witnessed. The measure of HaShem is that a person stumbles through a similar sin, but it is not the way of HaShem's measure to return silver to anyone's pouch — if so, we find a sinner being rewarded."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "The phrase כיוצא בעון is read as 'through a similar sin'; the logic is that they sinned by selling a brother into bondage and now face a parallel punishment."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:28.187735692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}